# HR Insight AI — Auth Endpoints
# Requires: REST Client VS Code extension
# How to use: click "Send Request" above any request block
#
# Backend runs on port 3010 (npm run start:dev)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3010
@contentType = application/json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# After login, copy the access_token value here
# ⚠️  NO quotes — paste the raw token string only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
@token = PASTE_YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### ✅ TEST 1 — Register a new user (should return 201 + token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}


### ❌ TEST 2 — Register duplicate email (should return 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}


### ❌ TEST 3 — Register with invalid data (should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short",
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "User"
}


### ✅ TEST 4 — Login as ADMIN (seeded user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ✅ TEST 5 — Login as HR Manager (seeded user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "hr.manager@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ✅ TEST 6 — Login as Team Manager (seeded user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "team.manager@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ❌ TEST 7 — Login with wrong password (should return 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}


### ❌ TEST 8 — Profile without token (should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile


### ✅ TEST 9 — Profile WITH token (paste token from TEST 4 above)
# 1. Run TEST 4 first
# 2. Copy the access_token value from the response
# 3. Paste it in @token at the top of this file
# 4. Send this request
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
